      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The acute myocardial infarction is a multi factor disease, and various risk factors participate in its occurrence and progression. Recently, many investigators have paid their attention to the genetic polymorphisms as new risk factors for coronary artery disease. These include the polymorphisms or mutations of the gene which relates to hypertension, diabetes, the platelet function, the property of the blood vessel, the blood coagulation fibrinogenolysis system, and serum lipids. The tendency toward the occurrence and progression of coronary artery disease might be decided genetically by combining these genetic polymorphisms."},
